id: ops-tk0h
title: A same-day re-release is blocked because the pinned pm-changelog rejects the -N version suffix
description: "The release job failed at Generate changelog and release notes with \"--date-from-version requires a calendar version in YYYY.M.D form; received 2026.9.6-1\", so nothing was published and npm stayed on the previous version.\n\nThe version scheme appends a -N suffix when a release already exists for the same calendar day, which is exactly what a second release on one day produces. pm-changelog 2026.8.17, the version this repository had installed, rejects that suffix. pm-changelog 2026.9.2 accepts it: its own error text reads \"optionally with a same-day -N suffix\", and running it here with --release-version 2026.9.6-1 --date-from-version exits 0 and writes the file, where 2026.8.17 exits 1.\n\nSo this is a stale dependency rather than a defect in either package. The declared range was already ^2026.8.17, which would resolve to 2026.9.2 on a fresh install, but CI runs npm ci and the lockfile pinned 2026.8.17. The declared range is not the binding constraint; the lockfile is.\n\nWorth recording because of how it surfaced. The release completeness audit had never executed - its gh calls carried no token - so the release job had reported failure on eight consecutive runs while publishing successfully. Giving that step its token made the job's status meaningful again, and the very next run surfaced this genuine blocker before publishing rather than after. A permanently red job cannot report a new failure; that is the whole cost of leaving one red."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 1
